# Generated proto JSON and sources stay LF so Windows autocrlf does not leave
# these trees permanently "modified" in `git status` (which makes lint-staged
# stash/restore on every commit). This does **not** change committed bytes and
# does not remove the ordinary trailing spaces `protoc-gen-es` emits on blank
# `//` comment lines — see ticket 05-proto-codegen-byte-stability.md.
data/proto/**              text eol=lf
packages/core/src/proto/** text eol=lf

# Root package.json flipped to CRLF once already (ticket 129) because nothing
# pinned it while core.autocrlf=false. Pin it the same way as the proto trees
# rather than widening to *.json, which would also catch data/ fixtures this
# ticket never measured.
package.json text eol=lf

# Everything text stays LF. Prettier via lint-staged rewrote 54 files to CRLF
# during the terminology cleanup, which turned a ~550-line diff into ~12,900 and
# reassigned blame for every line it touched. Ticket 129 was the same bug on
# package.json alone; pinning one file at a time did not stop it recurring.
* text=auto eol=lf
